### TITLE ###
NestedLeafPositionalAndInheritedFlag
### DESCRIPTION ###
A leaf's own args are positional; a namespace's args and the script's args
both reach it as flags, from anywhere on the path.
### INPUT ###
args:
    verbose v bool

command remote:
    timeout int = 30
    command add:
        name str
        url str
        calls fn():
            print("add name={name} url={url} timeout={timeout} verbose={verbose}")
    command remove:
        name str
        calls fn():
            print("remove name={name} timeout={timeout}")
### ARGS ###
remote
add
foo
https://x
--timeout=5
--verbose
### STDOUT ###
add name=foo url=https://x timeout=5 verbose=true

### TITLE ###
NestedInheritedFlagBeforeSubcommand
### DESCRIPTION ###
An inherited flag is accepted before the sub-command that consumes it, not
only after - it belongs to the namespace, which the user has already named.
### INPUT ###
args:
    verbose v bool

command remote:
    timeout int = 30
    command add:
        name str
        url str
        calls fn():
            print("add name={name} url={url} timeout={timeout} verbose={verbose}")
    command remove:
        name str
        calls fn():
            print("remove name={name} timeout={timeout}")
### ARGS ###
remote
--timeout=9
add
bar
https://y
### STDOUT ###
add name=bar url=https://y timeout=9 verbose=false

### TITLE ###
NestedInheritedDefault
### DESCRIPTION ###
A namespace arg's default reaches a descendant that never mentions it.
### INPUT ###
command remote:
    timeout int = 30
    command add:
        name str
        calls fn():
            print("add name={name} timeout={timeout}")
### ARGS ###
remote
add
foo
### STDOUT ###
add name=foo timeout=30

### TITLE ###
ThreeLevelNestingInheritance
### DESCRIPTION ###
Inheritance accumulates root-to-leaf across more than one namespace.
### INPUT ###
command a:
    one str = "1"
    command b:
        two str = "2"
        command c:
            three str
            calls fn():
                print("one={one} two={two} three={three}")
### ARGS ###
a
b
c
foo
--one=X
--two=Y
### STDOUT ###
one=X two=Y three=foo

### TITLE ###
DeeperCommandWinsNameCollision
### DESCRIPTION ###
When a namespace and its descendant declare the same arg name, the deeper
declaration wins - matching how Ra shadows inherited flags.
### INPUT ###
command outer:
    shared str = "from-outer"
    command inner:
        shared str = "from-inner"
        calls fn():
            print("shared={shared}")
### ARGS ###
outer
inner
### STDOUT ###
shared=from-inner

### TITLE ###
BareNamespaceErrors
### DESCRIPTION ###
A namespace has nothing of its own to run. The error names that namespace and
lists ITS sub-commands - not the root's, which is a different question.
### INPUT ###
command remote:
    timeout int = 30
    command add:
        name str
        calls fn():
            print("add")
    command remove:
        name str
        calls fn():
            print("remove")

command list:
    calls fn():
        print("list")
### ARGS ###
remote
### STDERR ###
Must specify a command for 'remote'

Usage:
  remote [command] [OPTIONS]

Commands:
  add
  remove

Global options:
      --timeout int        (default 30)
  -h, --help               Print usage string.
  -i, --interactive        Interactively prompt for script args not already provided, then run.
  -d, --debug              Enables debug output. Intended for Rad script developers.
      --color mode         Control output colorization. Valid values: [auto, always, never] (default auto)
  -q, --quiet              Suppresses some output.
      --confirm-shell      Confirm all shell commands before running them.
      --tls-insecure       Skip TLS certificate verification for all HTTP requests.
      --src                Instead of running the target script, just print it out.
      --reply line:value   Answer a prompt when there's no terminal. Repeatable; repeat a line to answer it again.
      --reply-na line      Assert a prompt won't be reached on this run; rad fails cleanly if it is.
### EXIT ###
1

### TITLE ###
NamespaceHelpListsSubcommands
### INPUT ###
